<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE lm6a-yaogan50-03 ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 6A / Yaogan 50-03 — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
thrust SL/vac interpolated on ambient pressure, mdot from Isp, staging/fairing/coast events; vertical rise to 14.0 s (rule: config guidance),
pitch kick 6.862 deg over 10 s, gravity turn, linear-tangent upper-stage steering tan(theta)=0.1238-0.000093*(t-t_ign), solved by optimizer.
Vehicle config: Long March 6A (sim/vehicles/lm6a.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
LM-6A: thrust/Isp/GLOW/booster count+size from Wikipedia; ALL propellant/dry masses DERIVED by budget closure or ASSUMED (none published). LOW confidence.
Flown: LL2 Success. Az 190 is a guess. LOW confidence.
Target (see launch config): insertion 500 km, apoapsis 500 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 190.00 deg; payload 3000 kg.
Pad: 38.858300N 111.580200E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-10-23T10:15:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: deploy time unpublished (CASC/SAST did not publish a payload-separation time for this flight). From insertion T+743.5 s the stage is propagated for TWO revolutions (osculating period 94.66 min) on the inferred insertion orbit (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model); rows tagged -coast.
POST-CUTOFF end T+12103 s: inferred insertion orbit, +2 revs (deploy time unpublished): alt 499.93 km, osculating 499.0 x 505.7 km, i 96.927 deg.</description>
